WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.065
A few numbers anchor the study.

00:00:02.145 --> 00:00:09.675
The empirical investigation covers two hundred and
seventy-eight distinct interventions in continuous control.

00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:13.411
The rollouts run over a horizon of one thousand steps,

00:00:13.491 --> 00:00:19.638
and the theory shows the error amplification
constant grows exponentially in that horizon.

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:21.091
On the language side,

00:00:21.171 --> 00:00:27.525
the models are two hundred and seventy million
parameter Transformers trained on TinyStories.

00:00:27.605 --> 00:00:35.689
The key contrast in the theory is that a
perturbation changes the behavior cloning loss by only order H delta squared,

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:41.085
but can change the rollout reward by order H times
e to the H delta minus one,

00:00:41.165 --> 00:00:42.400
an exponential gap.
